SUMMARY:Museum Makers: Exploring Cyanotype Through Nature
LOCATION:Hilliard Art Museum\, 710 E St Mary Blvd\, Lafayette
DESCRIPTION:Explore cyanotype\, a historic photographic process distinguish
 ed by its rich blue tones\, in a hands-on workshop with artist Jeni Battag
 lia Guidry . Using leaves\, flowers\, and found objects\, participants wil
 l experiment with composition\, texture\, and silhouette to create blue-an
 d-white prints through exposure to UV light. Finished prints will become h
 andmade greeting cards or bookmarks to keep or give.\n\nNo previous art ex
 perience is necessary. All supplies are included.\n\nMember Rate: $65 per 
 person\n\nNon-Member Rate: $75 per person\n\nAdvance registration is requi
 red\, as space is limited.\n\nhttps://hilliardartmuseum.org/event/museum-m
 akers-exploring-cyanotype-through-nature/
URL:https://hilliardartmuseum.org/event/museum-makers-exploring-cyanotype-t
 hrough-nature/
